  "applies_to": "Mitsubishi Electric 1100, 2033, 7011, 9800 and 9900 series UPS with the MUCM / Procon Mod-IP/50 Modbus interface, read by a BASgatewayLX.",
  "summary": "Gateway profile for Mitsubishi UPS through the MUCM interface: 74 objects (32 AI, 12 AO, 30 BI), 52 polled by default. It follows the UPS-MIB style layout: battery status, charge, seconds on battery, input and output values, output source (normal, battery, bypass, boost, reduce), bypass values and alarm bits; outputs hold nominal ratings, battery install date, audible alarm and test.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "Built from Contemporary Controls' BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile Mitsubishi_MUCM_1100_2033_7011_9800_9900_LX.csv; the profile maps the registers in the Procon MUCM Modbus register list (https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/MitsubishiProconMUCM.pdf).",
    "Object instances are the ones this profile assigns when it is loaded into the gateway. A site that edited or rebuilt the profile may use different instances.",
    "Only 52 of the 74 rows are flagged for polling in the profile; the rest are served only after you tick them in the gateway. Their descriptions say \"not polled by default\".",
    "The CSV has no read/write column: Analog/Binary Inputs are read-only and Analog/Binary Outputs are commandable (priority array), which is how the gateway maps them (access inferred). Descriptions give the Modbus register each object reads.",
    "Some names appear more than once in the profile as published (Bypass Voltage Phase BC); they are kept as printed and told apart by instance."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile Mitsubishi_MUCM_1100_2033_7011_9800_9900",
